From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:18:26 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-arcade

Neo Geo, CPS1 and CPS2 get a shelf each, Games/NEOGEO, Games/CPS1 and
Games/CPS2, on FinalBurn Neo (fbneo) alone. Platform::NeoGeo, Cps1 and
Cps2 are appended to SHELVES and Core::Fbneo to EVERY; upstream's ALL
lists stay as they are. A shelf lists .zip files, and the zip is the
romset FBNeo loads by path: it lists only when its name is a set of that
board in the pinned core, from slot_store::arcade's table
(arcade_sets.tsv, written by tools/arcade-sets.py from the pinned
source's driver structs). A zip that is not, the BIOS set neogeo.zip and
the Neo Geo system drivers included, is logged and left off.

The table also gives each set its full title, parent and orientation.
The title names the cart, sorts the shelf and drives the letter jumps
(Cart::shelf_name), so mslug.zip reads "Metal Slug - Super Vehicle-001";
the stem stays the set name, since FBNeo picks the driver from it.

Every policy method answers the arcade platforms explicitly and like
Mega Drive: L1 and R1 belong to the game (six-button CPS fighters), X
and Y pass through, no core picker, no crop, Stretch by default with a
4:3 choice, rewind on, the retro shader list. Neo Geo draws 320 or 304
wide on the 360x240 canvas and follows the frame width; CPS draws 384x224
on a 432x288 canvas, since a frame wider than its canvas would be
halved. A vertical arcade set drawn upright gets a 3:2 canvas as tall as
its long side. Shaders are kept in Config/neogeo_shader.txt,
cps1_shader.txt and cps2_shader.txt. Saves, States and Labels get the
three folders at boot. The shelves show the 32X cart until the arcade
shells land.
